# Generated by cyber-sandbox.
Port {{ ssh_port }}
PermitRootLogin no
PasswordAuthentication no
KbdInteractiveAuthentication no
PubkeyAuthentication yes
AuthorizedKeysFile {{ authorized_keys }}
AllowUsers {{ researcher_user }}
X11Forwarding no
AllowAgentForwarding no
# `claude ssh` carries the model API back to the host over a remote-forwarded unix
# socket, so remote forwarding is the one forwarding direction that stays on. Both
# keywords are needed for it: sshd gates a remote stream-local forward on the *TCP*
# remote permission as well, because `AllowTcpForwarding` is what
# `channel_disable_admin(ssh, FORWARD_REMOTE)` is derived from in session.c, and the
# socket request is then refused by the same admin check that refuses a TCP one. With
# `AllowTcpForwarding no` the socket is denied however this next line is set.
#
# Widening it to `remote` costs nothing here. Every forward is opened by the client, and
# the client is the host that holds the keys; the sandbox cannot ask for one. A remote
# forward only lets the host publish one of its own endpoints inside the sandbox, which
# is exactly what the agent socket is. Local forwarding stays off, so the host cannot
# use the sandbox to originate connections either.
AllowTcpForwarding remote
AllowStreamLocalForwarding remote
PermitTunnel no
PrintMotd no
AcceptEnv LANG LC_* ANTHROPIC_* CLAUDE_CODE_* CODEX_*
